cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nomos: Deterministic Execution Substrate and Transactional Git Worktree Layer for AI Coding Agents"
message: "If you use Nomos or its empirical verification benchmarks in your research or engineering systems, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gantlett
    given-names: Mark
    affiliation: SophiaLabs
repository-code: "https://github.com/mgantlett/nomos"
url: "https://sophialabs.ca"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24240539"
abstract: >-
  Nomos is an open-source static Go execution substrate that governs autonomous AI coding agents
  between local workspaces and production Git branches via read-only main locks, hermetic Git
  worktrees, 42 polyglot AST quality gates across 11 languages, diff-scoped mutation testing,
  CapBAC capability leases, Two-Phase Commit Git Notes provenance, and pure-Go SQLite episodic memory.
keywords:
  - ai-coding-agents
  - ast-verification
  - software-engineering-governance
  - git-worktree
  - mutation-testing
  - capability-security
  - brownfield-refactoring
license: Apache-2.0
